---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { computerObjects } from "../../data/computers";
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="Domain-joined computers" description="Browse the four recorded Active Directory computer objects and the separate VM/server systems they represent." breadcrumbs={[{label:"Directory",href:"directory/"},{label:"Computers"}]}>
<section class="page-head"><div class="container">
<div class="eyebrow">Identity / Computer accounts</div><h1>The computers known to the directory.</h1>
<p class="lead" style="margin-top:17px">A computer's Active Directory object identifies its domain membership and OU location. It is not the same as the virtual machine, its running services, or the physical Proxmox host.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container">
  <div class="card-list">{computerObjects.map(c=><a class="system-card" href={base+"computers/"+c.slug+"/"}>
    <small>Computer object · {c.ouSlug==="domain-controllers"?"Domain Controllers OU":c.ouSlug==="servers"?"Servers OU":"Workstations OU"}</small>
    <h3>{c.name}</h3><p>{c.purpose}</p><span class="readmore">Open domain computer profile →</span>
  </a>)}</div>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top:22px">The directory snapshot records <strong>four computer objects</strong>. Their VM hosts, nested virtualization and related services are explained separately in the linked system profiles. A policy link does not establish effective processing.</div>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
